xpf (0.0.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial xpf Debian package (increment A of #1917, subsumes #1923).
    Ships xpfd, xpf-userspace-dp, cli, the day-0 config-drive loader,
    and the systemd units. Binaries install to a dpkg-static staging
    path; live symlinks are created on first install only. The
    in-place upgrade cut-over mechanism is a separate increment.
  * The version field above is a placeholder; `make deb` rewrites it
    from `git describe` before building.
  * Keep transit forwarding closed when the armed bridge-family barrier
    leg is unsupported; reject malformed SSH authorized_keys entries at
    apply (#10725).
  * Install live-address host-input fences on #1960/#10297 fail-closed
    cold boots, preserving management addresses while blocking data addresses
    until a valid config can be applied (#10732).
  * Register day-0 and Debian maintainer-script regression tests with
    `make selftest` and census both test locations (#10747).
  * Mark subscriber-overrun gaps in CLI flow and packet-drop, gRPC packet-drop,
    and SSE streams, and expose flow-trace drop totals (#10834).
  * Report unknown interface duplex and surface counter/address read failures
    and unmatched interface filters in extensive interface output (#10843).
  * Include responder node identity in chassis-forwarding RPC responses and
    flag divergence between peer response identity and heartbeat belief
    (#10841).
  * Restrict `monitor traffic` to configured interfaces, require an explicit
    host-interface override, and report the requested and resolved capture
    devices (#10845).
  * Show config-sync divergence alarms without active configuration and report
    remote flow-monitor state as unknown (#10846).
  * Label cluster VRRP rows as configured and include per-group detail in
    gRPC cluster status (#10844).

 -- xpf maintainers <noreply@anthropic.com>  Mon, 16 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000
